# herdr config
#
# NOTE: This package is NOT stow-managed because ~/.config/herdr/ is a
# runtime directory where Herdr writes logs, sockets, and session state.
# Stow would symlink the entire directory, which breaks Herdr's file I/O.
#
# Instead, config.toml is symlinked individually:
#   ~/.config/herdr/config.toml → this file
#
# To set up on a new machine:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/herdr
#   ln -sf "$(pwd)/herdr/dot-config/herdr/config.toml" ~/.config/herdr/config.toml
